+The upstream commit is \texttt{6b162e80c59a}, with its full identifier in the logs. Three Conv1d declarations with two-dimensional kernels become Conv2d for PyTorch compatibility. Kernel size 2 and dilations $(1,2)$ per block give receptive field 13, requiring one left zero pad. The adaptive embeddings are 10-dimensional; graph convolution has order 2. Each 272,640-parameter checkpoint predicts nine slots; scoring uses the center. Inputs are centered by the float32 training-history global mean and divided by the global standard deviation plus $10^{-6}$. Validation is inverse-scaled and zero-clipped. Primary runs use FP32 channels-last storage. The six 30-epoch logs, weight digests and scalers agree: best epochs are 26/28/27 for Generated and 21/29/28 for Mixed, in seed order. The earlier layout runs remain separate.
 
